{"notes":["Position note (sto:init-standard-declaration): the ADR-023 embed mechanism — a root-level package with //go:embed over the module root (the skeletonembed precedent, revived by ADR-023 Decision 2 for the skill pack) — is ADOPTED as the distribution path for the EKA standard declaration file.","The EKA standard declaration (root `EKA`, compact consumer summary, `Version X.Y` line) is a cross-repo canonical source: it lives in the eka-standard repository and is vendored into eka-cli as a compile-time resource (standardembed, //go:embed EKA). The binary is the distribution vehicle — same rationale as ADR-023's skill pack (standalone portable binary, ADR-009; release-binary installs work without a checkout).","Consequences validated by implementation: `eka init` stays offline (no network code in bootstrap/; the file is embedded), dry-run stays deterministic (identical bytes every run), and the binary and the vendored standard travel together — the standard-corpus axis of `eka version` derives from the embedded `Version X.Y` line, locked to the conformance rules by a build-time consistency test.","Relationship to ADR-023: same mechanism, different purpose. ADR-023 distributes the AI Skill Pack (pack content); this position extends the mechanism to canonical standard sources. ADR-020 Decision 1 (identity-only init) is amended by the carve-out recorded in the ADR-020 amendment (instance :3).","Non-goals (unchanged): no network fetch at init, no checksum verification of the vendored asset, no --standard-version/--offline flags, no eka.yaml schema changes."],"role":"review","verdict":"approve"}